nSo the second condition failed. It failed because the left and right-sided limits are not equal:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)=2,\\,\\,{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)=3.\n$$\n\nThese limits both exist and are finite, yet they are not equal. Therefore, the discontinuity at $x=2$ is a jump discontinuity.\n\nConsequently, I is true, and II and III are false." 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307873 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307874 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307875 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307876 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307877 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1041 "selection" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307874 13194139534756 true] [17592186307872 1110 #uuid "008aafcf-5d72-5056-b337-44be156eac9c" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307873 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307873 1111 #uuid "bf22b19f-548b-5eab-98f3-1f873492f7dc" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307874 1034 "I only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307874 1111 #uuid "55c01282-b83a-5fd5-8adb-3cbcff29b2cf" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307875 1034 "III only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307875 1111 #uuid "63277236-585a-580d-bee0-d62bddfcbe9e" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307876 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307876 1111 #uuid "d815f591-412a-5394-a1bf-040363ef8624" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307877 1034 "II only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307877 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307877 1111 #uuid "64798606-8a72-5282-b35b-be61e6948047" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307878 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307879 13194139534756 true] [17592186307878 1089 "q-48112" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307878 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534756 true] [17592186307878 1100 "Given the functions $f(x),g(x)$ and $h(x)$ below, which of them has a jump discontinuity at $x=1?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}x+4, & x\\le 1 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+1, & x>1,\\end{aligned} \\\\ g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+1, & x<1 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+3}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned} \\\\ h(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x+3}, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}, & x=1,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307878 1113 #uuid "c3ff5938-5386-52c8-baaa-7140885bcc81" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307878 1145 "For $f(x),$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $f(1)=1+4=5$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}(x+4)=1+4=5\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}(3{x}^{2}+1)=3(1)^{2}+1=4.\n$$\n\nSo both the left and right limits exist and are finite, but they are not equal.$\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=1.$\n\nNow, for $g(x),$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $g(1)=\\sqrt{1+3}=2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}({x}^{2}+1)=(1)^{2}+1=2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}(\\sqrt{x+3})=\\sqrt{1+3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=2.\\,\\,✓$ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\n- Finally, we check that the value of the limit equals the value of the function: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}g(x)=2=g(1).\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=1.$\n\nFor $h(x),$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $h(1)=\\frac{1}{2}$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}\\frac{1}{x+3}=\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}\\frac{1}{x+3}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=\\frac{1}{4}.\\,\\,✓$ $\\,\\,\\,$\n\n- Finally, we check that the value of the limit equals the value of the function: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}h(x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\ne h(1).\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo the value of the limit does not equal the value of the function.\n\nTherefore, $h(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1.$" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307880 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307881 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307882 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307883 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307884 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1041 "selection" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307882 13194139534756 true] [17592186307879 1110 #uuid "103ca529-129c-538e-bf33-e84acd3fac78" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307880 1034 "$f(x)$, $g(x)$ and $h(x)$" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307880 1111 #uuid "b44cb702-8f3c-5b04-853e-bfabee62c659" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307881 1034 "$f(x)$ and $g(x)$ only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307881 1111 #uuid "7e3968dc-b090-5f57-ab40-db2960ec7307" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307882 1034 "$f(x)$ only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307882 1111 #uuid "bba64cc2-80b9-59d0-b4a6-7d13e912354c" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307883 1034 "$g(x)$ only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307883 1111 #uuid "25929590-3856-50c1-b9e9-a3186bd1bc7e" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307884 1034 "$h(x)$ only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307884 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307884 1111 #uuid "0ef59895-f90b-54c2-8f23-3eecda3fd45b" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307885 1017 #edb/ref 17592186307886 13194139534756 true] [17592186307885 1089 "q-48114" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307885 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534756 true] [17592186307885 1100 "Given the functions $f(x),g(x)$ and $h(x)$ below, which of them has a jump discontinuity at $x=0?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-3x, & x\\ne 0 \\\\ 0, & x=0,\\end{aligned} \\\\ g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}, & x\\ne 0 \\\\ 2, & x=0,\\end{aligned} \\\\ h(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}3, & x<0 \\\\ \\sqrt{x+4}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307885 1113 #uuid "c341ed7c-c896-5097-a1a6-74e007b32c66" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307885 1145 "For $y=f(x),$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $f(0)=0$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}({x}^{2}-3x)={0}^{2}-3(0)=0, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}({x}^{2}-3x)={0}^{2}-3(0)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=0.\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Finally, we check that the value of the limit equals the value of the function:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=0=f(0).\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0.$\n\nNow, for $y=g(x),$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $g(0)=2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1})=\\frac{1}{{0}^{2}+1}=1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1})=\\frac{1}{{0}^{2}+1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the overall limit exists and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}g(x)=1.$\n\n- Finally, we check that the value of the limit equals the value of the function: \n\n$$\ng(0)=2\\ne {lim}_{x\\to \\,0}g(x).\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo the value of the limit does not equal the value of the function.\n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=0.$\n\nFinally, for $y=h(x),$ let's go through our continuity checklist:\n\n- $h(0)=\\sqrt{0+4}=2$ exists $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Let's now check the left and right limits. We see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}h(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}(3)=3\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}h(x)={lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}(\\sqrt{x+4})=\\sqrt{0+4}=2.\n$$\n\nSo both the left and right limits exist and are finite, but they are not equal.$\\,\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, $h(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307887 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307888 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307889 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307890 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1000 #edb/ref 17592186307891 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1041 "selection" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1104 #edb/ref 17592186307891 13194139534756 true] [17592186307886 1110 #uuid "e09ca5b9-6e5f-57a6-bc4a-e53fd0094a8a" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307887 1034 "$f(x)$, $g(x)$ and $h(x)$" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307887 1111 #uuid "5a91ab59-2d52-5e73-878c-9d2392328831" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307888 1034 "$f(x)$ only" 13194139534756 true] [17592186307888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534756 true] [17592186307888 1111 #uuid "53a6b913-bad1-5f2d-a0eb-37929031c552" 13194139534756 tr